// Test: `·ed` / `·ing` must not swallow the head of a path segment
// Spec: 01-LEXICAL.md — aspect markers
// Priority: P1 — regression guard for defect S7
//
// `·ed` (perfective) and `·ing` (progressive) are aspect markers. logos resolves
// ambiguity by longest match, so `·edit` lexed as `·ed` + `it` and `·ingest` as
// `·ing` + `est`. Every path or method segment beginning "ed" or "ing" was hit.
//
// Exercised through method calls so the test checks real behaviour rather than
// only parsing — before the fix these did not resolve.

☉ Σ T { ☉ x: i64! }

⊢ T {
    ☉ rite edit(&self) -> i64! { ↩ 1; }
    ☉ rite ingest(&self) -> i64! { ↩ 2; }
    ☉ rite index(&self) -> i64! { ↩ 3; }
}

rite main() {
    ≔ t = T { x: 0 };
    println(t·edit());     // `·ed` must not eat "edit"
    println(t·ingest());   // `·ing` must not eat "ingest"
    println(t·index());    // `·ing` must not eat "index"
}
